This file documents all source-level patches applied to Wok and Kimchi
for Python 3.9+ compatibility. These patches are applied automatically
by install-kimchi-wok-py39.sh via sed/2to3 in-place edits.

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 1: Shebang lines
=======================================================================

All *.py files with "#!/usr/bin/env python" or "#!/usr/bin/python"
are updated to use "python3".

--- a/src/wok/server.py
+++ b/src/wok/server.py
-#!/usr/bin/env python
+#!/usr/bin/env python3

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 2: Module renames (Python 2 → Python 3)
=======================================================================

--- a/src/wok/*.py
+++ b/src/wok/*.py

ConfigParser (Python 2) → configparser (Python 3):
-import ConfigParser
+import configparser as ConfigParser

-from ConfigParser import SafeConfigParser
+from configparser import SafeConfigParser

httplib (Python 2) → http.client (Python 3):
-import httplib
+import http.client as httplib

urllib2 (Python 2) → urllib.request (Python 3):
-import urllib2
+import urllib.request as urllib2

-from urllib2 import urlopen, Request
+from urllib.request import urlopen, Request

urlparse (Python 2) → urllib.parse (Python 3):
-import urlparse
+import urllib.parse as urlparse

-from urlparse import urlsplit, urljoin
+from urllib.parse import urlsplit, urljoin

StringIO (Python 2) → io (Python 3):
-from StringIO import StringIO
+from io import StringIO

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 3: setup.py dependency names
=======================================================================

--- a/setup.py (Wok)
+++ b/setup.py (Wok)
-    'python-m2crypto',
+    'm2crypto',        # installed as python3-m2crypto system package

-    'python-cherrypy3',
+    'CherryPy',

-    'python-cheetah',
+    'Cheetah3',

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 4: DEBIAN/control dependency names (if using .deb path)
=======================================================================

If you are patching the pre-built 3.0.0 .deb (not the source install
path), apply the following control file changes:

--- a/DEBIAN/control (wok-3.0.0-0.debian.noarch.deb)
+++ b/DEBIAN/control
-Depends: python-m2crypto, python-cherrypy3, python-cheetah, ...
+Depends: python3-m2crypto, python3-cherrypy3 | python3-cheroot, python3-cheetah3 | python3-cheetah, ...

Rebuild command:
  dpkg-deb -b /tmp/wokfix /tmp/wok-fixed.deb
  sudo apt install -y /tmp/wok-fixed.deb

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 5: Wok CherryPy 18.x API compatibility
=======================================================================

CherryPy 18.x removed several deprecated aliases. If you encounter
AttributeError: module 'cherrypy' has no attribute 'quickstart':

--- a/src/wok/server.py
+++ b/src/wok/server.py
-cherrypy.quickstart(root, config=config)
+cherrypy.tree.mount(root, '/', config)
+cherrypy.engine.start()
+cherrypy.engine.block()

If you encounter issues with cherrypy.wsgiserver:
-from cherrypy.wsgiserver import CherryPyWSGIServer
+from cheroot.wsgi import Server as CherryPyWSGIServer

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 6: Cheetah3 template compilation
=======================================================================

Cheetah3 requires templates to be compiled. If you get NameError or
ImportError on .tmpl files:

  cd /opt/kimchi
  python3 -m Cheetah compile --nobackup src/kimchi/API.py.tmpl || true
  find . -name "*.tmpl" -exec python3 -m Cheetah compile --nobackup {} \; || true

=======================================================================
PATCH SET 7: libvirt Python 3 bindings
=======================================================================

The python3-libvirt package is required. If missing:
  apt install python3-libvirt

If lxml.etree is used for XML parsing (it is, in Kimchi):
  apt install python3-lxml

=======================================================================
NOTES
=======================================================================

- All patches preserve the original Apache 2.0 / GPL license headers.
- No binary reverse-engineering was performed.
- Source is publicly available at:
    https://github.com/kimchi-project/wok
    https://github.com/kimchi-project/kimchi
- The 2to3 tool (from python3-lib2to3 / python3 standard library)
  performs AST-level transformations that are safer than sed for
  complex Python 2 constructs (print statements, except syntax, etc.)
